# M / B013 — ef-core, git-workflow.

C R191 OL GOV-015 | MUST NOT | Do not commit, push, merge, rebase, reset, force-push, delete branches or perform other repository-changing Git operations unless explicitly requested; completing an implementation is not such a request. | Git operations | Explicit user request.
C R192 OL GOV-019 | MUST NOT | Never discard, overwrite, reset, clean or otherwise destroy user work to make a Git operation easier; do not automatically stash, reset or discard work to make a merge or rebase proceed; never remove a worktree containing uncommitted user work. | Git operations | none stated
C R193 OL GOV-020 | MUST | Before a repository-changing Git operation inspect the relevant repository state (git status, git diff, git diff --cached) and use the minimum operation required; do not silently clean up unrelated working-tree changes, rename existing user branches to satisfy a convention or push unrelated local commits accidentally. | Git operations | none stated
C R194 OL GOV-016 | MUST | Parallel implementation work uses separate branches or worktrees and keeps unrelated changes out of the current branch; one branch is not checked out in multiple normal worktrees and each worktree stays focused on its branch's concern. | parallel work | none stated
C R195 OL WF-022 | MUST | Before committing inspect the staged diff and include only the intended logical change; do not stage unrelated files merely because they are modified; implementation and its tests belong in the same logical commit; no artificial tiny commits and no unrelated fixes combined. | commits | none stated
C U2 LU GOV-015,GOV-020 | MUST NOT (high-risk) | High-risk Git operations (reset --hard, clean, push --force, push --force-with-lease, branch deletion, rebase of shared history) are performed only when explicitly requested or clearly required by an approved workflow, after inspecting what will be lost or rewritten. | Git operations | Clearly required by an approved workflow. | GOV-015 requires an explicit request for repository-changing operations; whether 'clearly required by an approved workflow' is an admissible substitute for that request cannot be decided from the oracle text. | An agent could run git clean or a force-push without a direct user request when it judges an approved workflow to require it.
C X18 EX GOV-015,GOV-020 | MUST NOT | main, master and other protected or shared branches are treated as non-rewritable; a shared branch is never force-pushed unless the user explicitly requests history rewriting and the consequences are understood. | push and history rewriting | Explicit user request for history rewriting of a shared branch. | GOV-015 requires an explicit request for force-push; the oracle does not declare named branches categorically non-rewritable. | A requested force-push to main is still refused or challenged under this rule.
C X19 EX WF-009,WF-022 | MUST | Run verify before preparing a pull request; the PR has a focused purpose and its description explains what changed, why, how it was verified and important compatibility or migration notes. | pull requests | none stated | WF-009 covers truthful verification reporting and WF-022 focused commits; the oracle does not prescribe PR preparation or description contents. | A PR description listing only file names does not follow the workflow.

